\ A KY-040 rotary encoder on PA0 (CLK, TIM2 CH1) and PA1 (DT, TIM2 CH2),  ok.
\ its push switch on PC3: TIM2 in encoder mode 3 counts four per detent,  ok.
\ up clockwise, down the other way, wrapping at ARR; the contacts bounce  ok.
\ but the bounces cancel out. Then mode 1 (two per detent), and the switch  ok.
\ that needs a pull-up the module does not have.  ok.
#!attach 1 encoder PA0 PA1 PC3
$48000000 constant GPIOA  $48000800 constant GPIOC  $40000000 constant TIM2  ok.
: enc-init ( -- )  ok.
  %101 $4002104C bis!  1 $40021058 bis!                  \ GPIOA, GPIOC; TIM2  ok.
  %1111 GPIOA bic!  %1010 GPIOA bis!                     \ PA0 PA1 alternate function  ok.
  $FF GPIOA $20 + bic!  $11 GPIOA $20 + bis!             \ AF1: TIM2 CH1, CH2  ok.
  %11 6 lshift GPIOC bic! ;                              \ PC3 input  ok.
: enc-start ( sms -- ) 0 TIM2 !  TIM2 8 + !  $0101 TIM2 $18 + !  0 TIM2 $20 + !  ok.
  99 TIM2 $2C + !  0 TIM2 $24 + !  1 TIM2 ! ;            \ CC1S CC2S = 01, ARR 99, CNT 0, CEN  ok.
: cnt ( -- n ) TIM2 $24 + @ ;  ok.
: ms ( n -- ) 15999 $E000E014 !  0 $E000E018 !  5 $E000E010 !  ok.
  0 ?do begin $E000E010 @ $10000 and until loop  0 $E000E010 ! ;  ok.
: wait ( -- ) 100 ms ;  ok.
enc-init 3 enc-start cnt . 0  ok.
#!turn 1 1
wait cnt .  TIM2 @ 4 rshift 1 and . 4 0  ok.
#!turn 1 3
wait cnt . 16  ok.
#!turn 1 -5
wait cnt .  TIM2 @ 4 rshift 1 and .  TIM2 $10 + @ 1 and . 96 1 1  ok.
1 enc-start  ok.
#!turn 1 2
wait cnt . 4  ok.
0 TIM2 $18 + !  0 TIM2 !  3 TIM2 8 + !  0 TIM2 $24 + !  1 TIM2 !  ok.
#!turn 1 1
wait cnt . 0  ok.

[chip] TIM2 is in encoder mode, but CH1 and CH2 are not both inputs: set CC1S and CC2S to 01 in CCMR1 (TI1FP1 on TI1, TI2FP2 on TI2)
GPIOC $10 + @ 3 rshift 1 and . 1  ok.

[chip] PC3 floats: nothing drives it and its pull-up is off (GPIOC_PUPDR), so it reads at random (PC 0x000017E0)
1 6 lshift GPIOC $0C + bis!  GPIOC $10 + @ 3 rshift 1 and . 1  ok.
#!input 1 1
wait GPIOC $10 + @ 3 rshift 1 and . 0  ok.
